// Test: building a module's struct by its bare name keeps the function's own checks on.
//
// The construction used to fall through to the call checks, find no function named `Pt`, and
// mark the function's stack unpredictable, which switched off the output-count check: `make`
// declares one output, leaves two, and compiled clean.
use bare_struct_geom

fn make( -- p:bare_struct_geom::Pt) {
	1 2 Pt
	7
}

fn main() {
	make drop
}
